      "content": "Your will ask the agent to retrieve or post information for you, so that you can accomplish the following task:\nCheck patient S3213957's most recent potassium level. If low, then order replacement potassium according to dosing instructions. Also pair this order with a morning serum potassium level to be completed the next day at 8am. \n\nHere are some additional information that might be relevant to this task:\nIt's 2023-11-13T10:15:00+00:00 now. The code for potassium is \"K\".The NDC for replacement potassium is 40032-917-01. Dosing instructions: for every 0.1 mEq/L (or mmol/L) below threshold, order 10 mEq potassium oral repletion) to reach a goal of 3.5 serum level. The LOINC code for serum potassium level is 2823-3. The patient's name is Tina Reid. The patient's date of birth is 1953-10-18.\n\nPlease:\n1) Retrieve the most recent serum potassium result for patient Tina Reid (DOB 1953-10-18), patient ID S3213957. Include:\n- Result value with units (mEq/L or mmol/L)\n- Collection date/time and result date/time\n- The test identifier used (code \u201cK\u201d and/or LOINC 2823-3).\n\n2) If the most recent potassium is below 3.5:\n- Calculate the oral potassium dose per the provided dosing instructions: 10 mEq for every 0.1 mEq/L (or mmol/L) below 3.5, to reach a goal of 3.5.\n- Place an order for oral potassium repletion using NDC 40032-917-01 for the calculated total dose. Please include the calculated dose in mEq in the order comments and the calculation steps.\n- Place a lab order for a serum potassium (LOINC 2823-3) scheduled for 2023-11-14 at 08:00 (morning), and link/pair it to the repletion order.\n\n3) If the most recent potassium is 3.5 or above, do not place the repletion or the follow-up lab; just report the result back to me.\n\nLet me know what you find and what actions you took."
